title: One provider adapter and a cancel-safe generation pipeline
---
date: 2026-10-17
---
author: Labyricorn
---
summary: A single OpenAI-compatible adapter detects Strata and LM Studio profiles, and the generation pipeline persists partial replies through cancellation.
---
tags: architecture, ai, sqlite
---
source_commit: f22bca79151e6907f299a60e050b5e43a2156c08
---
body:

Steps four and five turned registered endpoints into working conversations.

**Adapter.** One OpenAI-compatible adapter serves every endpoint. It detects
whether the server is Strata, LM Studio, or a generic service, normalizes each
profile's model list, parses streamed responses into a common set of events, and
maps failures onto a fixed set of error kinds. The request body is built from a
type that has no field for settings Labbonet must never send, so that guarantee
is a property of the code rather than of call-site discipline. A scriptable fake
provider supports repeatable tests.

**Pipeline.** A reply is recorded as a message plus a generation row that keeps
provenance: the model requested, the model the server reported, and timings.
Each endpoint has a concurrency limit enforced by a cancellable queue. A model
reported as not loaded needs explicit confirmation, because loading it could
evict another client's model.

Two lessons stand out. Writes meant to keep a partial reply cannot share the
context that was just cancelled, so they use their own deadlines; a test caught a
message stuck in the streaming state. And a live run found that a logging
wrapper had silently dropped the ability to flush streamed responses. Unit tests
bypassed the real middleware chain, so only driving the actual binary exposed it.

[Commit f22bca7](https://github.com/Labyricorn/Labbonet/commit/f22bca79151e6907f299a60e050b5e43a2156c08)
